| Term        | URI                          |
| ----------- | ---------------------------- |
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`      |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`        |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0` |
| `service`   | `org.dxos.mdl.service@1.0`   |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`      |
| `scenario`  | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`  |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`      |
| `decision`  | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0`  |

## Where things live

| What                                                   | Where                                   |
| ------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------- |
| Sessions, trajectories, the graph, snapshots, issues   | Lighthouse (its workspace), via the API |
| The Research object: goal, budget, link to the session | ECHO, in the space                      |
| Picks and kept results, as immutable `Finding`s        | ECHO, the Research's feed               |
| Votes and stars                                        | ECHO tag index, and sent to lighthouse  |
| Rating adjustments                                     | Lighthouse (the session's overrides)    |
| The connection (server URL and API token)              | ECHO, as a plugin-connector Integration |

Everything else the article shows (every result, the live thread, extension sections, the rating model) is
read live from the API and not copied.

## Types

```mdl
type Research
  desc: >
    A goal handed to a lighthouse search session. Links to the session by run id on one lighthouse
    connection; holds what the person kept as an append-only feed of Findings.
  fields:
    name?:      string
    goal:       Prose
    budget?:    Budget                  # minutes, usd, pages (lighthouse-api Budget)
    connection: Ref<Integration>        # the lighthouse server it runs on
    run?:       string                  # the lighthouse session; set once it starts
    feed:       Ref<Feed>               # immutable Finding entries (SetParent)
    tags:       Ref<TagIndex>           # starred and voted Findings (SetParent)
    lastSeq?:   number                  # the trajectory seq the feed was last synced to
    lastRunAt?: string                  # ISO 8601
  annotations:
    icon: ph--binoculars--regular
    hue: amber
    label: name
```

```mdl
type Finding
  desc: >
    One result copied out of lighthouse into the space: the entity's identity and current facts at the time
    it was kept, with where they came from. Immutable; keeping it again after the facts change appends a
    newer entry with the same iri.
  fields:
    iri:        string                  # the lighthouse subject
    title:      string
    url?:       string
    types:      string[]                # CURIEs, e.g. schema:Restaurant
    images:     string[]
    properties: Record<string, unknown> # CURIE → values, as lighthouse returns them
    provenance: FindingSource[]
    score?:     number                  # the rating score when kept
    why?:       Prose                   # the agent's reason, for a pick
    keptBy:     pick | person
    keptAt:     string                  # ISO 8601
  annotations:
    icon: ph--push-pin--regular
    hue: amber
    label: title
```

```mdl
type FindingSource
  fields:
    extractor: string                   # id@version
    source?:   string                   # the page or API it read
    at:        string
```

## Components

```mdl
component ResearchArticle
  desc: >
    Article surface for a Research. Two panes, as lighthouse's own web UI: left, the session's trajectory as
    the assistant ChatThread (prompts, one tool panel per answer, result pills, the report as pick cards)
    with a composer that sends follow-ups; right, the results as a masonry of FindingCards ranked by the
    session's rating model, with the rating model panel behind the toolbar's model button. Before the
    session starts it shows the goal and budget form.
  props:
    research: Research
  state:
    stream: connecting | live | lost
    showModel: boolean
  actions:
    start()                             # op:StartResearch
    send(text)                          # op:SendToResearch
    stop()                              # op:StopResearch
```

```mdl
component FindingCard
  desc: >
    A result in the masonry: photos and map, title, the key facts by kind, the score, thumbs up/down, a keep
    toggle, and the result's extension sections with a "More about this" menu (quick read or research).
    Renders a live lighthouse entity, or a kept Finding when the connection is offline.
  props:
    entity: Entity | Finding
    research: Research
  emits:
    onVote(vote: up | down | clear)
    onKeep(kept: boolean)
    onExtend(extension: string, deep: boolean)
```

```mdl
component RatingModelPanel
  desc: >
    The session's rating model term by term (what each reads, its formula with the session's numbers, its
    share), with a nudge and an on/off switch per term and requirement; ported from lighthouse's web UI.
  props:
    research: Research
```

```mdl
component LighthouseMeta
  desc: >
    A settings surface for one connection: its status and version, plugins and what they contribute, the
    vocabulary, issues (with triage), and storage (bytes by area, prune, cache clear).
  props:
    connection: Integration
```

## Services

```mdl
service LighthouseClient
  desc: >
    The typed lighthouse-api client, bound to one Integration (server URL and token). Runs wherever the
    plugin's operations run; on the desktop app it talks to the local daemon directly, in a browser over
    HTTPS to the same localhost or a hosted server.
  loading: lazy
```

```mdl
service LighthouseSidecar
  desc: >
    Desktop only. Runs the lighthouse daemon as a Tauri sidecar with its workspace in the app's data
    directory, the way plugin-claude runs dx-agent, and registers it as the default connection.
  loading: lazy
```

## Operations

```mdl
op StartResearch
  key: org.dxos.operation.lighthouse.start
  desc: Creates the lighthouse session for a Research (createSession) and records its run.
  input:
    research: Ref<Research>
  output: Ref<Research>
  effects: [http, echo:write]
  requires: [LighthouseClient]
```

```mdl
op SendToResearch
  key: org.dxos.operation.lighthouse.send
  desc: A follow-up into the session (sendMessage, from composer).
  input:
    research: Ref<Research>
    text: string
  effects: [http]
  requires: [LighthouseClient]
```

```mdl
op StopResearch
  key: org.dxos.operation.lighthouse.stop
  input:
    research: Ref<Research>
  effects: [http]
  requires: [LighthouseClient]
```

```mdl
op SyncFindings
  key: org.dxos.operation.lighthouse.sync
  desc: >
    Appends to the Research's feed every pick in the session's report that is not in it yet, and records
    lastSeq. Runs when the stream reports the session reported, and on open.
  input:
    research: Ref<Research>
  output: number                        # Findings appended
  effects: [http, echo:write]
  requires: [LighthouseClient]
```

```mdl
op KeepFinding
  key: org.dxos.operation.lighthouse.keep
  desc: Copies one result into the feed (getEntity with provenance) and stars it.
  input:
    research: Ref<Research>
    iri: string
  output: Finding
  effects: [http, echo:write]
  requires: [LighthouseClient]
```

```mdl
op VoteFinding
  key: org.dxos.operation.lighthouse.vote
  desc: Records the vote in the tag index and sends it to lighthouse (sendFeedback), which rebuilds the model.
  input:
    research: Ref<Research>
    iri: string
    vote: up | down | clear
  effects: [http, echo:write]
  requires: [LighthouseClient]
```

```mdl
op ExtendFinding
  key: org.dxos.operation.lighthouse.extend
  desc: Reads one extension for one result (extend); deep starts a child session, shown as a link.
  input:
    research: Ref<Research>
    iri: string
    extension: string
    deep?: boolean
  effects: [http]
  requires: [LighthouseClient]
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Connection

  req F-1.1: The plugin registers a plugin-connector IntegrationProvider for lighthouse with a credential form (server URL, API token); the token is an AccessToken.
  req F-1.2: On the desktop app the sidecar's daemon is the default connection, with no form.
  req F-1.3: A connection that does not answer shows offline: the article shows kept Findings and the last synced state, read-only.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Research

  req F-2.1: A Research is created from the space's create menu or by the assistant, with a goal and a budget preset (Quick, Standard, Deep).
  req F-2.2: Starting it creates the lighthouse session and stores its run; the article streams it from then on.
  req F-2.3: The thread is steering only: results appear on the right, and the report's picks appear as pick cards.
  req F-2.4: A follow-up sent from Composer is marked from composer; follow-ups from the CLI or lighthouse's own UI appear live.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Findings in the space

  req F-3.1: When the session reports, its picks are appended to the feed as Findings with keptBy pick.
  req F-3.2: Keep on a card appends the result as a Finding with keptBy person and stars it; unkeep removes the star, not the entry.
  req F-3.3: Findings are immutable; the feed is the Research's history of what was kept.
  req F-3.4: Members of the space see the Research and its Findings without a lighthouse connection of their own.
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Ranking and facets

  req F-4.1: The masonry ranks by the session's rating model with the person's adjustments, as lighthouse's web UI does.
  req F-4.2: Votes are kept in the tag index and sent to lighthouse.
  req F-4.3: The rating model panel adjusts the session's overrides through the API.
  req F-4.4: Extensions that apply to a result are offered on its card; a deep one links to its child session, which is a Research of its own only if opened.
```

```mdl
feat F-5: The assistant

  req F-5.1: A skill gives the assistant lighthouse's MCP tools (search, entity, sparql, extend) and an operation to start a Research for a goal.
  req F-5.2: The assistant hands research goals to a Research instead of searching itself, and answers from its Findings.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Offline Research
  given: a Research with kept Findings; its connection does not answer
  when: a member opens it
  then:
    - the article shows the Findings as cards and a connection-offline notice
    - the composer and votes are disabled
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: Picks are kept once
  given: a Research whose session reported 8 picks, 3 of them already in the feed
  when: SyncFindings runs
  then: 5 Findings are appended, with keptBy pick
```

## QA

```mdl
test QA-1: Research a goal from Composer
  desc: The round trip through the API, against a local lighthouse daemon.
  actors: both
  covers: [F-1.1, F-2.1, F-2.2, F-3.1, F-4.2]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - a lighthouse daemon is running locally, with its API token at hand
  steps:
    - name: Connect lighthouse
      do: In Settings → Integrations, add Lighthouse with the local URL and the API token.
      expect: the connection shows online with lighthouse's version
    - name: Start a Research
      do: Create a Research with the goal "Board game cafés in Bangkok with a big game library" and Quick budget, then start it.
      expect: the thread shows the goal and the agent's first tool runs; result cards appear on the right
    - name: Vote and keep
      do: Thumbs-up one card, and press keep on another.
      expect: the kept card's Finding is in the Research's feed; lighthouse's feedback for the session lists the vote
    - name: Wait for the report
      do: Wait until the session reports.
      expect: the picks appear as pick cards and as Findings with keptBy pick
```

## Open questions

- Web-only Composer users: a local daemon reached from the browser, a hosted lighthouse, or both.
- Whether every result should be kept automatically (larger spaces, offline-complete) rather than picks and
  the person's keeps.
- plugin-commerce: its Provider templates (a request mapping and CSS/JSONPath result mapping written by an
  LLM) could become a lighthouse extractor kind, with commerce searches run by lighthouse's runSearch; or
  this plugin replaces it.

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: Composer is lighthouse's web UI: a Composer plugin reaches lighthouse through its API, while lighthouse's code stays in its own repository.
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: user:dmaretskyi
```

```mdl
decision D-2: The plugin adds a Research object linked to one lighthouse session; its article is lighthouse's two-pane view (the assistant ChatThread steering on the left, the ranked masonry on the right) reading the session live from the API. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  why: Lighthouse's web UI is already built from the same DXOS components, so the view ports with its behavior intact.
```

```mdl
decision D-3: The session's picks and the results a person keeps are copied into the space as immutable Findings in the Research's feed, with provenance; everything else is read live and not copied. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  why: Copies are what members without a connection see and what outlives the lighthouse workspace; copying every result (hundreds per session) would fill spaces with what nobody chose.
  rejected: Copying every result; copying nothing (a Research unreadable without the person's own lighthouse).
```

```mdl
decision D-4: The connection is a plugin-connector Integration with the API token as an AccessToken; on the desktop app a Tauri sidecar runs the lighthouse daemon and is the default connection. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  why: plugin-connector already stores credentials and renders the setup; plugin-claude's dx-agent is the precedent for a local server beside the desktop app.
```
